+---
+title: resolve_color_default is keyword-only (override=)
+author: HarzerHeribert
+date: 2026-10-15
+cost: { minutes: 1, tokens: 25211 }
+touches:
+  - src/click/globals.py
+  - src/click/termui.py
+  - src/click/utils.py
+---
+
+## Decided
+- `click.globals.resolve_color_default` signature is `(*, override: bool | None = None) -> bool | None`. Callers pass `override=color`; behavior unchanged (explicit value wins, else current context's `ctx.color`, else None).
+- Callers: `utils.echo`, `termui.get_pager_file`, `termui.progressbar` (pass `override=color`); `termui._readline_prompt` and `exceptions.ClickException.__init__` call it with no args.
+
+## Tried and ruled out
+- Nothing in tests/, docs, or .pyi stubs references the helper, so no test/doc changes were needed.
+
+## Watch out
+- Any new caller must use the keyword `override=`; positional or `color=` raises TypeError.
+- In zsh, an unmatched glob like `*.rst` aborts the whole command line; quote globs or use `grep -r --include`.
